r (53)", "Coding verdicts split; Antigravity (Ultra-only) ≫ Gemini CLI", "Standout for writing & 3D/multimodal; “2026 model, 2025 harness”"], "eps": [{"t": "What Gemini 4 Argon Is Actually Good For", "url": "https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-10-14", "d": "Oct 14"}]}], "harness": [["Claude Code", "Anthropic", ">$2.5B", "run‑rate · Feb (official)", "Claude"], ["Cursor", "Anysphere", "~$4B", "annualized · Jun (reported)", "Own: Composer 2 (Kimi K2.5 base)"], ["Codex", "OpenAI", "5M+", "weekly users · Jun (official)", "GPT"], ["Devin / Windsurf", "Cognition", "~$1B", "run‑rate · late Sep (reported)", "Own: SWE‑2"], ["Lovable", "Lovable", ">$600M", "ARR · Sep (TechCrunch)", "Claude Opus 5.5 / Fable 5.1"], ["Replit", "Replit", "~$525M", "ARR · Apr (estimate)", "Multi: Fable 5.x, GPT‑6 Astra"], ["OpenClaw", "OpenClaw Fdn", "392k ★", "GitHub stars · Oct 18", "Any (bring your own)"], ["Hermes Agent", "Nous Research", "255k ★", "GitHub stars · Oct 18", "Any + own Hermes 4"], ["v0", "Vercel", "6M+", "users · Mar (reported)", "—"], ["Bolt.new", "StackBlitz", "$40M", "ARR · Mar 2025 (old)", "Mostly Claude (reported)"]], "matrix": {"cols": ["Claude", "GPT", "Gemini", "Grok", "Chinese open", "Local", "Own model"], "rows": [["Claude Code", "●", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["Codex", "", "●", "", "", "", "", ""], ["Cursor", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "", "● Composer 2"], ["Devin / Windsurf", "○", "○", "○", "", "", "", "● SWE‑2"], ["Lovable", "●", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["Replit", "●", "●", "", "", "", "", ""], ["OpenClaw", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", ""], ["Hermes Agent", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "● Hermes 4"], ["Perplexity", "○", "○", "○", "○", "○", "", "● Sonar"], ["Bolt.new", "●", "", "", "", "", "", ""]]}, "coverage": {"All sections": "curated by hand for the Oct 18 edition from live sources (see links)"}, "caveats": ["Unlock % are Grok Bot estimates from access tier, harness, effort defaults and habits, anchored on Anthropic's Claude Code study (novice ~15% vs expert ~28–33% verified success). No cross‑lab study measures this.", "Moved since Oct 12: Google is now rated on Argon (public Oct 13) instead of 3.8 Flash: everyday 30–45 (app access is Pro/Ultra only; free tier stays on Flash), researcher 55–70 (Antigravity is Ultra‑only and testers quoted by AI Daily Brief saw big gaps between harnesses). Meta now rated on Muse Wonder: 60–75 / 30–45 (Muse Code + API; heavy plan‑limit complaints at launch). Earlier moves (Sep 21 → Oct 12): OpenAI everyday 30–45, Anthropic researcher 70–85.", "Usage: ChatGPT >1.2B weekly (OpenAI); Gemini app >1B monthly (Google, Aug); Grok ~117M monthly AI‑feature users (SpaceX S‑1, Mar); Claude app ~56M monthly (Reuters/Sensor Tower, Jun). Mobile DAU figures via BofA/Sensor Tower are secondary. Codex + Work \"40M active\" has no stated window.", "Argon public Oct 13 (API paid tier, AI Studio, Gemini app/AI Mode for Pro & Ultra, Antigravity for Ultra): intro $2/$10 until Nov 30, then $4/$20. 3.8 Flash $0.75/$3.75; Astra $10/$50. Grok 4.6‑high #73 · 1454 on Arena. Opus 5.5 fast mode left research preview Oct 15.", "AI Daily Brief notes paraphrase Nathaniel Whittemore’s episode transcripts (aidailybrief.ai, Sep 22 – Oct 16), incl. reactions he quoted; commentary, not data. This week: Oct 13 (Muse Wonder: frontier benchmarks, split real‑work reviews), Oct 14 (Argon), Oct 16 (MAI‑Base‑2 and Muse Spark Open as the week’s overlooked enterprise story).", "Full landscape (Oct 18): one row per company's latest/best model. Arena = LMArena Text Oct 15 (416 models); AA = Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index Oct 18 (best effort setting). * = AA partial estimate. Meta = Muse Wonder (API, $4/$20, Oct 12); Muse Wonder Full is Muse Code subscription‑only, AA 56 and 68.0% Coding Agent, not on LMArena. Meta open = Muse Spark Open (816B/42B active, Oct 15, Muse Model License with limited commercial terms, not yet on LMArena; $1.25/$4.25 hosted per modeldrops). Kimi K3 & Hy3 counted open‑weight per AA/licence. Mistral Large 4 is a proprietary preview. Microsoft MAI‑Thinking‑1, ByteDance Seed, Baidu ERNIE AA, Perplexity Sonar and SSI have no public text‑leaderboard score; Microsoft's MAI‑Base‑2 (2.8T/80B active, Oct 15) is a base model still in post‑training. DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 (Oct 17, open weights) has vendor benchmarks only; row shows prior V4.1 Flash scores. NVIDIA's Nemotron 3.5 Super VL (Oct 15) scores AA 26 but only 1416 (prelim) on Arena; row kept on Nemotron 3 Ultra. Coding Agent % for Kimi K3, GLM‑5.3, Qwen3.8 Max and Step 5 come from AA's Coding Agent Index (various harnesses).", "SSI: still no model, paper or API as of Oct 18; $32B valuation (Apr 2025 round) and ~$5B Nvidia investment (Jul 27, Bloomberg‑reported size). Rumoured August model did not ship. Thinking Machines: Inkling (975B/41B active, open weights, Jul 15) + Tinker fine‑tuning platform. Perplexity retired Sonar Chat Completions Sep 27; Agent API routes to OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI, Z.AI, Moonshot, NVIDIA plus Sonar. ARR >$450M (Mar, FT via secondary tracker).", "Harness figures are mixed quality: official = Claude Code >$2.5B run‑rate (Feb 12), Codex 5M+ weekly (Jun 2). Secondhand/estimates = Cursor ~$4B (Jun), Cognition ~$1B (Sep), Replit ~$525M (Apr), v0 6M+ users, OpenClaw 3.2M MAU (SimilarWeb est.). Claude Code ~$15B “tracked ARR” is a third‑party estimate, not shown. Lovable >$600M ARR via TechCrunch. Bolt $40M is Mar 2025, no newer figure. Lovable/Bolt model stacks are third‑party reporting. Hermes = Nous Research’s Hermes Agent (open source) + Hermes 4 models.", "Capability overhang: ceiling = AA Intelligence; reach = ceiling × midpoint of unlock estimate. Argon now public (was reach 0). Meta Muse Wonder (60–75/30–45) and MiMo (65–80/15–30: open weights + cheap API, little consumer surface) are derived estimates. MiMo beats Grok 4.7 (both 46) on LMArena rank.", "xAI: no new text model; Grok Voice 3.0 (Oct 14) ranks #1 on AA's Speech‑to‑Speech Index (86.9, per x.ai citing AA). Grok 5 preview reported Oct 14 with no release date; API still tops out at grok‑4.7. OpenAI: no new text model this week; GPT‑Live‑1.1 voice models rolled out in ChatGPT Oct 15.", "Vendor benchmark tables treated as claims; LMArena and Artificial Analysis are independent."], "links": [{"t": "x.ai Grok 4.7", "url": "https://x.ai/news/grok-4-7"}, {"t": "docs.x.ai", "url": "https://docs.x.ai/developers/grok-4-7"}, {"t": "GPT‑6.1 Sol", "url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-1-sol"}, {"t": "Sol docs", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol"}, {"t": "GPT‑6 for everyone", "url": "https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-for-everyone/"}, {"t": "DevDay recap", "url": "https://openai.com/index/devday-2026-recap/"}, {"t": "TechCrunch", "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/29/openai-launches-gpt-6-1-sol-says-it-nearly-matches-gpt-6-astra-and-costs-less/"}, {"t": "Opus 5.5", "url": "https://www.anthropic.com/claude-opus-5-5"}, {"t": "Sonnet 5.5", "url": "https://www.anthropic.com/claude-sonnet-5-5"}, {"t": "Haiku 5.5", "url": "https://www.anthropic.com/claude-haiku-5-5"}, {"t": "Gemini 4 Argon (Sep 30)", "url": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-4-argon/"}, {"t": "LMArena Text", "url": "https://arena.ai/leaderboard/text"}, {"t": "Argon public (Oct 13)", "url": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-argon/"}, {"t": "Muse Wonder (TechCrunch)", "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/12/meta-releases-its-first-frontier-model-muse-wonder/"}, {"t": "Muse Wonder dev blog", "url": "https://dev.meta.ai/resources/blog/build-with-muse-wonder"}, {"t": "Muse Spark Open", "url": "https://research.meta.ai/blog/muse-spark-open"}, {"t": "MAI‑Base‑2", "url": "https://microsoft.ai/news/frontier-pre-training-at-microsoft-ai/"}, {"t": "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017", "url": "https://the-decoder.com/deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017-beats-larger-rivals-in-agentic-tasks-while-once-again-massively-cutting-per-ta